  view_file {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///skills/system_skills/github_import_migration/references/web.md"
    end_line: 149
    content: "# Web Migration (Node.js Runtime) \342\200\224 Self-Contained\n\nThis file contains ALL instructions for migrating web projects to AI Studio.\nRead top-to-bottom. Do NOT navigate to other reference files.\n\n## AI Studio Web Constraints\n\n- **Runtime**: Node.js 22, npm only. No yarn, pnpm, bun.\n- **Port**: 3000 is the ONLY accessible port. Host must be `0.0.0.0`.\n- **Entry**: `npm run dev` must start the app on port 3000.\n- **Filesystem**: Ephemeral \342\200\224 container sleeps \342\206\222 disk wiped.\n- **Networking**: HTTP(S) outbound only. Direct TCP to external databases is\n  blocked. Exception: Cloud SQL uses Unix Domain Sockets.\n- **Container**: linux-x64 (Node.js 22-slim). No native compilation tools.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 1: Project Normalization\n\n### 1.1 Package Manager\n\n- DELETE: `yarn.lock`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `bun.lockb`, `bun.lock`,\n  `.yarnrc.yml`, `.yarnrc`, `.pnpmfile.cjs`\n- DELETE: `.DS_Store` files (recursive) \342\200\224 macOS metadata, must not be committed\n- KEEP: `package-lock.json` (if present)\n- Remove `\"packageManager\"` field from package.json\n- Remove `\"preinstall\": \"npx only-allow ...\"` scripts\n- Resolve `catalog:` version specifiers to real versions\n- Convert `\"resolutions\"` \342\206\222 `\"overrides\"` (npm format):\n  `\"resolutions\": { \"webpack/terser\": \"5.31.0\" }` \342\206\222\n  `\"overrides\": { \"webpack\": { \"terser\": \"5.31.0\" } }`\n- Rewrite ALL `yarn`/`pnpm`/`bun` commands in scripts, Makefile, Procfile:\n  `yarn <script>` \342\206\222 `npm run <script>`, `pnpm exec` \342\206\222 `npx`, `bunx` \342\206\222 `npx`\n- If `install_applet_dependencies` fails with peer conflicts \342\206\222\n  `shell_exec npm install --legacy-peer-deps`\n\n### 1.2 Node Version\n\n- DELETE: `.nvmrc`, `.node-version`\n- If `engines.node` excludes 22: update or remove\n\n### 1.3 Monorepo Detection\n\nIF `turbo.json`, `nx.json`, `lerna.json`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, or\n`\"workspaces\"` in package.json, OR `apps/`/`packages/` with own package.json:\n\n1. Keep workspace structure intact. Do NOT flatten.\n2. Pick the most deployable app (priority: Next.js > Vite/React > Express > any with `dev` script)\n3. Ensure root package.json has `\"workspaces\": [\"apps/*\", \"packages/*\"]`\n4. Delete `pnpm-workspace.yaml`. Map `\"workspace:*\"` \342\206\222 `\"*\"` in deps.\n5. Wire root dev script: `\"dev\": \"npm run dev --workspace=apps/<chosen>\"`\n6. Keep `turbo.json`/`nx.json` if present (they work with npm)\n\n### 1.4 Deno / Bun Runtime\n\nIF `deno.json`, `bunfig.toml`, `bun.lockb`, or source contains `Deno.serve`,\n`Bun.serve`, URL imports:\n\n**Delete**: `deno.json`, `deno.jsonc`, `bunfig.toml`, `bun.lockb`, `bun.lock`\n\n**Create/update package.json** with `\"type\": \"module\"` and dev script.\n\n**Convert ALL runtime APIs using this table:**\n\n| Deno/Bun API | Node.js Replacement |\n|---|---|\n| `Deno.serve(handler)` | `express()` + `app.listen(3000, \'0.0.0.0\')` |\n| `Deno.readTextFile(path)` | `fs.promises.readFile(path, \'utf-8\')` |\n| `Deno.writeTextFile(path, data)` | `fs.promises.writeFile(path, data)` |\n| `Deno.env.get(\"KEY\")` | `process.env.KEY` |\n| `Deno.openKv()` | In-memory `new Map()` |\n| `Bun.serve({ port, fetch })` | `express()` + route handler |\n| `Bun.file(path)` | `fs.promises.readFile(path)` |\n| `Bun.write(path, data)` | `fs.promises.writeFile(path, data)` |\n| `Bun.env.KEY` | `process.env.KEY` |\n| `Bun.password.hash(pw)` | `bcryptjs.hash(pw, 10)` \342\200\224 install `bcryptjs` |\n| `Bun.password.verify(pw, hash)` | `bcryptjs.compare(pw, hash)` |\n| `Bun.hash(data)` | `crypto.createHash(\'sha256\').update(data).digest()` |\n| `Bun.sleep(ms)` | `new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, ms))` |\n| `Bun.Glob` | `glob` npm package |\n\n**Convert frameworks:**\n\n| Source Framework | Convert To |\n|---|---|\n| Oak (Deno) | Koa (NOT Express \342\200\224 Oak is a Koa clone) |\n| Fresh (Deno) | Next.js |\n| Elysia (Bun) | Fastify |\n| Hono | Keep Hono \342\200\224 add `@hono/node-server` |\n\nIf project uses TypeScript without a build step, add `tsx`:\n`install_applet_package([\"tsx\"], isDevDependency=true)` and\n`\"dev\": \"tsx watch src/index.ts\"`\n\n### 1.5 Non-Node.js Languages\n\nIF primary runtime is Python, Go, Ruby, PHP, Java, or other (no package.json):\n\n1. Analyze: catalog endpoints, models, templates, auth, env vars\n2. Pick target framework:\n   - Pure API \342\206\222 Express or Fastify\n   - Fullstack with \342\211\2455 templates \342\206\222 Express + EJS\n   - Fullstack with <5 templates \342\206\222 Next.js\n3. Rewrite core 3-5 routes with in-memory data (`Map`/`Array`, NOT real ORMs)\n4. Stub remaining routes with `res.status(501).json({ error: \'Not yet migrated\' })`\n5. Use language conversion tables below for syntax mapping\n6. **CRITICAL CLEANUP**: After successfully creating and compiling the Node.js app, you MUST delete the original source files and configs (e.g., `.py`, `.go`, `requirements.txt`, `pyproject.toml`, `Makefile`, `compose.yml`, `alembic/`) to avoid polluting the repository and confusing build rules. Keep only `README.md` and `LICENSE`.\n\n**Python \342\206\222 Node.js**: `@app.route` \342\206\222 `router.get`, `request.json` \342\206\222 `req.body`,\n`request.args.get` \342\206\222 `req.query`, `jsonify(data)` \342\206\222 `res.json(data)`,\n`Blueprint` \342\206\222 `express.Router()`, `Depends()` \342\206\222 Fastify hooks\n\n**Django/Rails/Laravel \342\206\222 Express+EJS**: Models \342\206\222 in-memory Map/Array,\n`{% extends %}` \342\206\222 `<%- include(\'header\') %>`, `@foreach` \342\206\222 `<% for() { %>`\n\n**Go \342\206\222 Node.js**: `c.JSON(200, data)` \342\206\222 `res.json(data)`, `c.Param(\"id\")` \342\206\222\n`req.params.id`, goroutines \342\206\222 synchronous inline\n\n### 1.6 Infrastructure Artifacts\n\n- Do NOT delete Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, fly.toml \342\200\224 scan for env vars\n- Extract env vars into `.env.example`\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 2: Dependencies\n\n### 2.1 Native Addons\n\n| Package | Action |\n|---|---|\n| `sharp`, `esbuild`, `@swc/core`, `re2`, `@node-rs/*`, `fsevents` | KEEP |\n| `bcrypt` | SWAP \342\206\222 `bcryptjs` |\n| `argon2` | SWAP \342\206\222 `@node-rs/argon2` |\n| `node-sass` | SWAP \342\206\222 `sass` |\n| `canvas`, `puppeteer` | STRIP + comment out imports |\n| `cpu-features`, `microtime` | STRIP |\n\nFor unlisted native addons: try `install_applet_dependencies` first. If\n`node-gyp` / `gyp ERR!` / `make: not found` \342\206\222 STRIP and comment out imports.\n\n### 2.2 Database & Data Layer \342\200\224 MOCK IMMEDIATELY\n\nScan deps for: `pg`, `postgres`, `mysql2`, `mongoose`, `mongodb`, `redis`,\n`ioredis`, `better-sqlite3`, `prisma`, `drizzle-orm`, `typeorm`, `sequelize`,\n`knex`, `bull`, `bullmq`, `kafkajs`, `amqplib`.\n\n**IF ANY found \342\206\222 apply the matching mock template NOW:**\n\n#### Redis / KV (`redis`, `ioredis`)"
    num_lines: 410
    num_bytes: 16203
    line_range_bytes: 6342
  }
}
