  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Static Website Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `website/public` directory. It looks like a complete static website. There\'s an `index.html` file, which is expected. I\'m also finding other pages there, such as `get-started/index.html`, `first-investigation/index.html`, and `showcase/index.html`. It appears to have subdirectories, like `showcase/aeg`.\n\n\n**Expanding Website Structure Analysis**\n\nI\'ve discovered many more files within the website\'s structure. It now looks like there are several guides, examples, a FAQ, a blog, and contributor sections. The `assets` directory contains CSS, JavaScript, and figure assets. I\'m moving on to exploring the `morluto/rea` repository for more context now.\n\n\n**Considering Static Website Integration**\n\nI\'m now contemplating integrating the static website directly. Could we copy it into the workspace and serve it? Even better, what about serving the static website while simultaneously providing an interactive REA Explorer/REA Agent API bridge? This would create a truly dynamic and interactive experience.\n\n\n"
