  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Sync Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on ensuring the HTML title, description, and Open Graph metadata in `index.html` are synchronized with `metadata.json`. My key thought is to replace the default content in the HTML entry point with the data from the JSON file, or that the JSON file can override the HTML. I am specifically considering `<title>`, `<meta name=\"description\">`, `og:title`, and `og:description` tags, so that the main entry point is well structured for social sharing, search engine optimization, and website metadata overall.\n\n\n**Defining Website Architecture**\n\nI am now structuring the architecture based on the desired website experience, focusing on content categorization. I need to outline the main sections such as Home, Guides, Showcases, Getting Started, First Investigation, Interactive Dino Lab, Notes Web inspection, FAQ, and Blog. Each area will have subsections. I\'m prioritizing user experience and navigation.\n\n\n**Integrating Interactive Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating an Interactive REA Agent and Reverse Engineering Studio as a central component. I\'m focusing on a persistent action bar for quick access to tools such as a disassembler/hex inspector, a live OTP/hash calculator, the Dino Speed & Physics Lab, a CTF Mask Solver, and an MCP Tools Catalog Explorer. The tools will allow users to quickly paste or load snippets of hex strings for analysis.\n\n\n"
