  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Architecture and UX**\n\nI\'m now diving into the serving architecture and user experience. I\'ve begun reviewing the guidelines and constraints, specifically focusing on the requirements for the development server (port 3000) and avoiding browser alerts. Additionally, I\'m analyzing the metadata.json structure, with emphasis on the naming, descriptions and permission settings.\n\n\n**Evaluating User Interaction**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user interaction and how the application will handle requests to `http://localhost:3000/`. The use of `server.ts` with Express is being considered. I\'m exploring how Express can serve static assets and handle potential backend routes. Ultra mode\'s build, verify, critique, and fix loop is now actively guiding my approach to ensure a robust and testable application.\n\n\n**Defining Website Routes**\n\nI\'m now mapping out the website\'s structure, focusing on how different pages from `rea_site` will be served. I\'m thinking about how the backend APIs, like `/api/mcp-catalog` and `/api/solve-ctf`, will be designed and implemented. I\'m also considering the integration of the REA Interactive Bar/Explorer Navigation, including its placement and functionality.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Functionality Adherence**\n\nI\'ve just revisited the `github-import-migration` rules. The directives are now crystal clear: zero styling changes, no new features, and the primary goal is functional preservation. These constraints are paramount. I\'ve also checked `rea_site/index.html` and confirmed it\'s the official `morluto/rea` website, complete with its authentic CSS. The next step is to explore serving it directly on port 3000, checking for any conflicts.\n\n\n**Implementing Server Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating `server.ts` with Express. I\'ve considered how it will serve static assets, specifically `rea_site/index.html`, and handle potential API endpoints, including AI Studio requirements. I\'m investigating how to handle the synchronization of title and meta descriptions from `metadata.json` with the HTML entry point, and ensuring that assets are correctly served. I\'m also exploring options for the structure of the root directory.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_965321"
