  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Vite\'s Behavior**\n\nI\'ve been noticing how Vite handles static assets during the build process of `index.html`. It appears that when a script tag uses an absolute path like `/assets/theme.js`, and that file also exists in the `public/assets/theme.js` directory, Vite wisely leaves the public assets untouched. It seems to smartly avoid bundling those files starting with `/`.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1110179"
