    combined_output {
      full: "<truncated 23 bytes>\n network loss. Prefer detail summary, then kind qlog trace/stream  pages; select one trace, stream ID and direction for contribution/range pages.  Facts retain all-recorded-events-before-selection scope. Other qlog layouts  and PCAP correlation are unsupported.- User-owned Electron runtime already open: `list_electron_targets`. Before an electron-main Inspector attempt, check packaged fuses with `inspect_electron_fuses`; disabled `EnableNodeCliInspectArguments` means the app ignores `--inspect`.- Packet-field discovery: `inspect_packet_fields` searches installed protocols  and field names/types before choosing fields for `inspect_packet_capture`.  Query/page the relevant records; registrations do not establish observed traffic.- Recorded packet captures: `inspect_packet_capture` with selected TShark fields,  display filters and decode-as rules. Requires Linux, util-linux prlimit and  TShark 4.x on an absolute `PATH` entry or via the optional absolute  `REA_TSHARK_COMMAND` override; see  [capture guide](https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/packet-captures.md).  Packet limits count input packets before filtering. Output defaults to 50 matching  frames; use `match_offset` / `match_limit` for later pages, or explicit null  limit for complete matching output. Preserve the source digest across pages.  This does not perform live capture.  For address/DNS/SNI/protocol summaries use `inspect_pcap_capture` with MCP  detail summary, then retained kind pcap pages. Requires Wireshark 4.x tshark  and capinfos, with Linux prlimit or Windows Job Objects; see  [packet summaries](https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/pcap-analysis.md).  Select an exact DNS question for address pages; page exhaustion does not prove  network completeness. This reads recordings and does not acquire traffic.- Decoder discovery: `inspect_signal_decoders` searches installed decoder IDs  or selected decoder help, including channels and options. Query and page the  relevant details before choosing settings; this does not scan hardware.- Recorded logic/signal traces: `decode_signal_recording` with explicit decoder,  channel and protocol settings. On Linux with util-linux prlimit, supply sigrok-cli 0.7.2 through  `REA_SIGROK_COMMAND`; see [recording guide](https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/signal-recordings.md).  Output defaults to 50 literal lines; select annotation classes and page with  `line_offset` / `line_limit`, or explicit null for all remaining output.  Window counts are display lines, not annotations or samples. Preserve source digests across pages.  This reads existing files; it does not acquire hardware signals.- Explicit local WebAssembly artifact: `inspect_wasm_artifact`. Supply WABT 1.0.42  through `REA_WABT_BIN_DIRECTORY`; retain exact byte/tool identity and decoded WAT.  Select JavaScript glue and candidate paths explicitly and preserve URL/path  ambiguity. No implicit fetch or target execution; WAT is not original source.  See the [WASM guide](https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/wasm-artifacts.md).- Explicit local Android APK (or ZIP/AAB) signing: `inspect_apk_signature`.  Prefer its summary or selected signer/digest/lineage page; retain complete  Evidence and use `inspect_analysis_view` kind `apk-signature` for follow-ups.  Reports which schemes are present (v1 JAR, v2, v3, v3.1), each signer\'s  certificate SHA-256 fingerprint (v1 included, from its PKCS#7 block), v3 key-rotation lineage, source stamp, and  whether each signed digest still matches the bytes (self-consistency). This  is identity and integrity, not a trust or authenticity verdict.  See the [APK signature guide](https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/apk-signature.md).- Explicit local EVM bytecode carrier: `inspect_evm_interface` with caller-selected  `raw` or `hex` encoding. The owned worker deadline is `timeout_ms` (default  30000 ms, range 1..2147483647, next call). It does not raise the fixed byte,  address-space, or CPU allowances. Preserve carrier/decoded digests and treat selectors,  argument strings and mutability as inferred candidates; this performs no chain  lookup or target execution. For the complete inferred interface without hex or  duplicate stdout, discover support and select `detail: \"summary\"`; complete  Evidence stays retained under its original identity. Use the returned  `parent_evidence_id` for exact function or `bytecode_hex`/stdout/stderr pages.  Candidate coverage does not establish interface completeness. See the  [EVM bytecode guide](https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/evm-bytecode.md).- Embedded Go compiler, module or build-setting metadata: `inspect_go_binary`  with the explicit local file. This built-in target-free inspection requires no  Go installation or disassembler. Preserve raw module bytes and source ranges;  absent metadata does not prove a binary is not Go, and unparsed text records  remain explicit. See the  [Go binary guide](https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/go-binaries.md).- Embedded CUDA/HIP code objects: `inspect_gpu_code_objects`; inventory targets  first, then decode selected payloads and query retained GPU Evidence.- Bundled GGUF or safetensors model declarations: `inspect_model_artifact`  with the explicit local file. Default header hashing leaves full-file identity  unknown; `hash: \"full\"` additionally reads all weights for SHA-256. MCP returns  retained summaries; optional `view` selects one page in the initial call. Use  `inspect_analysis_view` kind `model-artifact` for  batched metadata keys, tensor names or type totals, selected fields and pages.  Preserve header-scoped indices and array preview omissions; do not infer model  behavior from declared architecture or tensor types. See the  [model file guide](https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/model-artifacts.md).- Unity IL2CPP names, member owners and string literals from `global-metadata.dat`:  `inspect_il2cpp_metadata` with the explicit local file; MCP defaults to compact  counts. Query sections, images, types, methods, fields, properties, events,  parameters or string_literals through `inspect_analysis_view`  with the returned `parent_evidence_id`, using exact filters, batch indices and  selected fields. Parameters accept `method_indices`, avoiding a scan of all  parameter pages. Missing collections in historical Evidence remain unknown.  Versions 24, 27, 29, 31 and 39; no Unity, IL2CPP  binary or disassembler is run. Unrecognized magic (possibly encrypted) and  other versions are unsupported. Optional matching `binary_path` enables static native addresses and type references; query `method_addresses` with indices or addresses/states, preserving every shared-body method and both artifact identities. Without a linked binary native counts remain unknown. Byte-pattern fallback is inferred; no runtime behavior or same-build pairing is proved. See the  [IL2CPP metadata guide](https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/il2cpp-metadata.md).- Embedded cargo-auditable Rust dependency metadata: `inspect_rust_binary`  with the explicit local ELF, PE, or thin Mach-O file. This built-in  target-free inspection requires no Rust installation or disassembler. Preserve  package order, dependency indices, and the section file range. A missing  `.dep-v0` section is null metadata, not proof the binary has no dependencies.  A rustc commit hash is an inference from a read-only `/rustc/<40-hex>/` path.  For selected crates, use `view: {collection: \"packages\", names: [...],  fields: [\"name\", \"version\", \"source\"]}` on the first call; explicitly include  `dependencies` for direct index references. Use `detail: \"summary\"` for counts  and ranges, or retained `inspect_analysis_view` Rust package/edge pages for  subsequent filters. Keep the complete parent Evidence accessible; CLI compact  delivery requires `--evidence_output`.  See the  [Rust binary guide](https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/rust