    combined_output {
      full: "<truncated 24 bytes>\nether. Each input retains its own snapshot, digest and byte-rangeprovenance; inputs and recovered code are never executed. Recovery requires acaller-supplied Wakaru on Linux x64; see [the recovery guide](https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/javascript-recovery.md).Use `analyze_javascript_application` directly on the operator-supplied ASAR orextracted tree. When the question concerns known source paths and the connectedschema advertises `source_paths`, select exact inventoried paths such as`[\"package.json\", \"main.js\", \"preload.js\"]`. Include supporting manifests orsource maps explicitly; dependencies are not implicitly analyzed. REA retainsthe complete artifact inventory and identity but reads source text and analyzesonly selected files. The result and summary record `source_selection`; filesoutside scope and their relationships remain unknown, so partial applicationcoverage does not mean the selected source failed. Use repeated `--source-path`on either static application CLI route, or `--source-paths-json` with a JSONfile for selections too long for one command line. Omit the selection when thequestion requires complete application analysis; `source_paths: []` is invalid,not an unfiltered request. `detail: \"summary\"` reduces deliveryand does not by itself reduce analysis work.==> /tmp/skills-use-fIKy6z/reverse-engineer-anything/references/native-and-artifacts.md <==# Native, managed, and packaged artifactsFor release comparisons on one MCP connection, retain `list_procedures` Evidencefrom each target and reuse its exact IDs after target switches or `close_binary`.For a handoff or new process, export the complete bundle and import it there,including its source closure. `reset_investigation` explicitly clears retainedrecords; optional `save_path` checkpoints them before clearing.`match_native_functions` pairs unique exact names and, when supplied,complete observed body bytes. Reuse optional same-context `list_names`,`procedure_info`, `read_bytes` and existing `analyze_function` dossiers as`left_observations`/`right_observations`; an MCP `analyze_function` summaryreply contributes its `parent_evidence_id` as a `retained-evidence` reference,not the summary itself. Avoid decompiling every function merely to match it. Its summary retains a parent for`inspect_analysis_view` `function-matches` collections `matches` and `functions`.Select columns, batch IDs and page individual facts; aliases remain unresolved.Unpaired observations do not prove additions/removals. Existing matched dossierpairs include inputs for `compare_functions`; otherwise analyze just chosen pairs.Aggregate completed comparisons with `find_changed_behavior`, selecting eachcomparison\'s exact `retained-evidence` ID instead of resending full records.Inline comparison Evidence remains accepted. References belong to the currentserver: after handoff, import the original bundle including its source closure.Do not substitute dossier IDs or summary views. Static differences remainbehavior candidates, with runtime behavior unknown unless separately observed.==> /tmp/skills-use-fIKy6z/reverse-engineer-anything/references/runtime-observation.md <==# Runtime observation## Native runtime questionsStart from the requested observation. State the selected target, input, expectedresult, failure signal and stopping condition before a run. Reuse static Evidenceto choose a function or hypothesis; `trace_native_values` follows recoveredstatic value dependencies and does not measure runtime values. Prefer staticinspection or existing capture comparison when it already answers the question.| Question                                                                               | Existing workflow                                                                                                                            | Host and effects                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      || -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- || Which selected native entry is reached, with which integer argument registers?         | `observe_native_calls` on the active Mach-O, with exact function/Objective-C breakpoints and a duration/event bound                          | macOS with LLDB and required debugger access. Launches a new owned process, stops at entries, records and continues; target execution may write files, show UI or use the network. It never attaches to an existing process. Inspect termination and partial coverage after the run.                                                                  || What does caller-authored instrumentation observe?                                     | `list_frida_devices` / `list_frida_processes` when discovery is needed; `start_frida_session`, `load_frida_script`, then status/unload/close | Requires compatible installed Frida bindings and selected device access; the real REA verifier covers Linux. Attach selects an existing PID; spawn selects a program and starts it paused until `resume_frida_session`. Scripts execute in the target and can change memory, files, network activity and behavior. This is not passive inspection.    || Which debugger state or controlled execution explains the behavior?                    | `start_gdb_session` and `gdb_console`, or `start_rizin_debug_session` and `rizin_debug_command`                                              | Persistent debugger workflows are Linux-only. GDB starts a debugger; console commands choose/load/attach/run targets. Rizin debug start launches the selected target and requires a durable `inferior_tty`. Both consoles are unrestricted and can change target memory/registers, run shell commands, write files and use the network.               || How do terminal output, process lifetime and selected files differ between runs?       | `capture_process_scenario`, then `compare_process_captures` with compatible recorded inputs                                                  | New captures require Linux or macOS and a working native PTY backend; macOS also needs `xcrun`/Swift for ownership inspection. Capture launches an owned command with ordinary user permissions. Observation paths select snapshots, not a filesystem sandbox. Comparing retained captures does not execute targets and is also available on Windows. || What does an existing desktop window show, or what changes after a declared UI action? | `observe_native_ui`; use `capture_native_ui_scenario` only for requested actions                                                             | macOS 14+ with required Screen Recording/Accessibility access. Select an existing PID/window. Observation does not launch or own the app; scenario actions can change its data or trigger network activity, and leave its state as-is.                                                                                                                |Close each persistent session with its matching tool. `close_frida_session`unloads scripts and detaches; it does not kill the target. A still-paused spawnis resumed only after instrumentation cleanup is confirmed. GDB and Rizin closecan detach a live inferior and let it continue only after verifying its durableoutput terminal. When disposition or cleanup is unresolved, preserve the ownedsession and reported recovery; do not assume that closing the debugger terminatedthe target. Process capture and LLDB call observation instead own their launched"
    }
