  run_command {
    cwd: "/app/applet"
    exit_code: 0
    blocking: true
    wait_ms_before_async: 3000
    combined_output {
      full: "<truncated 23 bytes>\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 || Missing, malformed or stale registration                        | Prepare a scoped setup plan; apply only authorized changes with backups.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                || Aligned registration, but no connected tools                    | Restart/reconnect the client. Doctor checks registration; it cannot establish the current agent\'s connection. Inspect the client\'s launch error if reconnection fails.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  || MCP connection dropped or REA could not start                   | If the connection drops, retry that call once only when it is safe to repeat or known not to have started. If it may already have changed the target, or the same failure returns, tell the user REA\'s connection failed and ask them to restart the MCP client. If REA could not start its connection, retry once, then tell the user and ask them to restart the MCP client. Do not retry a startup failure that returns the same unchanged result. Run `rea doctor` when REA could not start or tools stay missing after restart. Doctor cannot restore a live connection by itself. || `MCP tool call requires approval, but approval policy is never` | Codex rejected the call before REA executed it. Do not install an engine or repeat setup to solve this client-policy decision. See the approval section below.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          || REA returns `provider_unavailable` or an unavailable tool entry | Read that operation\'s provider diagnostics or `binary_session.result.tool_availability`. Expand each group\'s tool names and inherit the shared client requirements unless overridden. Use the operation\'s availability, reason, and remediation; a complete tool catalog does not imply every operation is available. Request `{\"detail\": \"complete\"}` only for provider diagnostics.                                                                                                                                                                                                   |==> /tmp/skills-use-fIKy6z/reverse-engineer-anything/references/evidence-workflows.md <==# Evidence, comparison, and verification workflowsEvidence-producing tools return the complete Evidence record directly in MCP`structuredContent` and CLI JSON. Read `normalized_result` for operation data,and cite `evidence_id` when another tool or your explanation needs a stablereference. Preserve authority, limitations, coverage, and residual unknowns. If a resultis incomplete or paginated, continue only when the remaining data matters tothe task; do not fetch a bundle or resource merely to read a result alreadyreturned inline. When complete `inspect_binary_layout` or`analyze_javascript_application` Evidence is already retained, call`inspect_analysis_view` for a summary, one section/symbol/module, or a stablepage instead of repeating the producer.For any logical Evidence source that advertises retained references, pass`{kind: \"retained-evidence\", evidence_id}` instead of copying the completerecord back into a call. The same contract covers individual, optional, arrayand nested sources across native, process, JavaScript, managed, mobile and WASMworkflows. Sources can independently mix inline records and exact references.Resolution preserves the source\'s identity, provenance, coverage, partial factsand unknowns; it neither reruns analysis nor makes incomplete facts complete.Keep domain role and identity requirements: a native dossier cannot substitutefor a managed member observation, for example.When starting from a summary or inspection page, use its`normalized_result.parent_evidence_id` to reference the complete source.==> /tmp/skills-use-fIKy6z/reverse-engineer-anything/references/environments.md <==# Agent environments from a live applicationUse this when the user asks for an agent environment (an AgentEnv bundle) of aweb application: a folder `agent-env` deploys, whose MCP tools answer from whatone recording of the application observed and serve the writes that recordingconfirmed. The workflow records the application once with`capture_browser_scenario`, checks what the environment would serve, recordsagain if a hint names a gap, then writes the bundle with`export_environment_bundle`. For a HAR the user already has, skip to[export](#export-and-hand-off) through `inspect_web_network_capture`, or use`rea environment-build <capture.har> <dir>`.## Before recording- Record only against an instance the user says is disposable or seeded for  this purpose: every write step creates, edits or deletes its data. If the  user has not said so, ask before any scenario that writes. REA does not  start, seed or reset applications.- Credentials come from environment variables the user names. Declare each as a  scenario secret, `{secret_id, environment_variable}`; the variable must be set  in the environment REA\'s MCP server started with. Never ask for a password in  chat. Declared secrets are redacted as the capture records.- Map the application first with `inspect_web_page` (and `capture_web_screenshot`  when layout matters): the login form\'s locators, and the API calls behind the  pages that list and edit the entities the user asked about.==> /tmp/skills-use-fIKy6z/reverse-engineer-anything/references/android-applications.md <==# Android application artifactsUse the connected server\'s advertised Android tools. Repository main and npm4.1.0 include this family. A skill installation alone cannot add it to anolder server.Start with `inspect_android_package` on the caller\'s APK path for packageidentity, manifest declarations, coverage, and inline Evidence. Use`search_android_classes` to find candidates, `inspect_android_class` for oneclass\'s members, `inspect_android_method` for decompilation, and`trace_android_references` for incoming static references. Each call takes itsown APK path and explicit selectors; do not open a native session first.Choose an `overload_index` from the class inventory when methods are ambiguousinstead of guessing.For JNI implementations, discover `inspect_android_jni_bindings`. Select rawDEX class/method identities and optional descriptors, ABI or logical librarypaths. Prefer `detail: \"summary\"`; complete Evidence remains retained and`android-jni` views page declarations, libraries, candidates or binding rowswith exact fields. Global native-pair ambiguity survives class selection.Preserve slot/relocation provenance and source coverage: matched means observedcandidate presence; partial scans do not establish uniqueness or absence.This reads DEX/ELF bytes without loading the APK into the decompiler or executingtarget code. Runtime registration and loading remain unknown. See the[JNI guide](https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/android-analysis.md#link-native-declarations-to-jni-candidates)."
    }
