  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Interface Changes**\n\nI\'ve been looking over OmeTV\'s loading sequence, specifically at the entrance modal. It\'s switched from \"OmeTV member\" to \"Stream+ member,\" complete with a custom retro-style logo. The hero image on the left, showing a happy user video, remains, however. This indicates a definite shift in the branding, and my focus is on analyzing the implications.\n\n\n**Analyzing Login Options**\n\nI\'m now examining the login options, noticing the \"Continue with FB,\" \"Google,\" and \"Email/Guest\" choices, alongside the VK ID option. The age verification and user agreement confirmation are standard. There\'s a close button, suggesting a \"Continue as Guest\" feature. I\'m focusing on how these choices affect user onboarding and engagement. The green \"\342\227\217 397,096 users online\" gives a feeling of popularity.\n\n\n**Detailing Interaction Elements**\n\nI\'m now detailing the individual interactive elements. A \"Stop\" button uses brown/red, and an Esc key alternative is noted. Country selection uses flag dropdowns. Gender identity options include \"Guy,\" \"Girl,\" and \"Couple.\" The real-time chat panel shows system safety, message logs, and an input box with emojis. I see a top header with the Stream+ logo, an online counter, language selection, and links to rules and safety.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1101590"
