  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing UI Components**\n\nI\'ve successfully passed all six tests, which is great! My current focus is on building the React UI components for Stream+. First up: `src/components/StreamHeader.tsx`. I\'m starting with a TV logo badge. It\'ll have an orange/red retro TV silhouette and bold \"Stream+\". I\'m also including a real-time online counter with a pulsating green dot: \"Online\".\n\n\n**Adding Interactive Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating more interactive elements. I\'ve designed a sound toggle button with audio feedback, a keyboard shortcuts guide accessed via modal (F2/Space, Esc, M, V), and triggers for Rules & Safety and a Member/Sign-in button. I\'m moving on to building the `RemoteVideo` component, aiming for a dynamic, high-definition simulated video avatar with realistic animations and environmental backgrounds. I\'m focusing on overlay badges, status banners, interactive like reactions, and a report button for that component. Then I\'ll focus on `LocalVideo.tsx`.\n\n\n**Designing Video Controls**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `RemoteVideo` and `LocalVideo` components, integrating permissions for the live video stream. If access is denied or the environment is headless, I\'ll render a simulated webcam test pattern with the user\'s avatar, volume visualizer, and label. For controls, I\'m implementing mic mute with visual mic level, camera toggle, background blur simulation, and a fullscreen toggle. Then I\'m working on the chunky bottom control dock.\n\n\n**Implementing Chat Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating the chat functionality. I\'m focusing on an auto-scrolling message container that will include system events, messages from strangers with avatars and country flags, and my own messages with distinctive speech bubbles. I am also implementing quick action prompt chips and a message input field with an emoji tray toggle, and a send button. I also am working on system rules and safety reminder messages. I\'m also planning to incorporate a ban system for rule violators, with facial visibility requirements.\n\n**Building the Auth Modal**\n\nI\'ve moved on to the authentication modal. I\'m constructing a replica of the OmeTV modal, but branded for \"Stream+.\" It will feature a high-quality image banner with the online user count on the left side, and the Stream+ TV logo along with options to continue with Google, Facebook, or Email, as well as a prominent \"Start as Guest\" button on the right side.\n\n\n"
